## 8. Product Details
- Show large product image, product name, flavor, description, price, rating, quantity selector, Add to Cart, Favorite and related products. The page must be responsive.

---

## 9. Shopping Cart
- Customers can add/remove products, increase/decrease quantity, view subtotal and total, continue shopping and proceed to checkout.
- Use frontend state. Example: Chocolate Fudge Rs. 220 × 2 + Mango Magic Rs. 220 × 1 = Rs. 660 subtotal. Mock delivery may be Rs. 100, giving Rs. 760 total.

---

## 10. Checkout
- Frontend-only form with Full Name, Phone Number, Email, Address, City and Payment Method.
- Mock payment options: Cash on Delivery, Card, Easypaisa and JazzCash.
- After Place Order, show a success message and generate a mock order number. No real payment processing.

---

## 11. Offers
- **Happy Hour**: 20% OFF, 4 PM–6 PM.
- **Double Scoop Deal**: Rs. 320.
- **Family Combo**: 4 scoops + 2 shakes — Rs. 1,150.
- **Weekend Special**: Buy 2 sundaes and get 1 topping free.

---

## 12. Responsive Chatbot — ScoopBot
- Floating chatbot button visible throughout the website.
- **Desktop**: bottom-right expandable chat panel.
- **Tablet**: automatically resized chat panel.
- **Mobile**: large/full-screen responsive chat interface without breaking the website.
- **Chatbot header**: ScoopBot 🍨 with subtitle “Your sweet assistant”.
- Include bot avatar, close/minimize controls, chat messages, text input, send button, typing indicator, timestamp, scrollable conversation and reset conversation.

---

## 13. Chatbot Welcome & Quick Actions
- **Welcome**: “Hi! I'm ScoopBot 🍨 How can I help you today?”
- **Quick actions**: View Menu, Check Prices, Popular Flavors, Today's Offers and Recommend Something.

---

## 14. Chatbot Functionality
- Answer common questions using predefined rules/mock data.
- Examples: list available flavors; identify the cheapest product; recommend chocolate products; find products under Rs. 300; recommend a product; answer mango availability.
- Recommendations should display product image, name, price, short description and an Add to Cart button.

---

## 15. Chatbot Responsive Requirements
- Work on desktop, laptop, tablet and mobile.
- Never overflow outside the screen.
- Keep messages readable and the input accessible.
- Support scrolling through long conversations and touch-friendly controls.
- Test approximately at 1920px, 1440px, 1024px, 768px, 390px and 375px widths.

---

## 16. About & Contact
- **About**: fictional brand story, mission, values, quality statement and team section.
- **Contact**: contact form, phone, email, shop address, opening hours, social icons and map placeholder.
- **Hours**: Monday–Sunday, 11:00 AM–11:00 PM.

---

## 17. Navigation & Interactions
- All major buttons should work: Menu, Order Now, Add to Cart, Cart, Product Details, Checkout, Chatbot, category filters, search and favorites.
- Recommended chatbot products must be addable to the cart.

---

## 18. State Management
- Use frontend state for shopping cart, product quantities, favorites, search, filters, chatbot messages and chatbot open/closed state.
- Local storage may optionally preserve the cart after refresh.

---

## 19. Responsive Design
- Desktop: full navigation, multi-column product grids and spacious layouts.
- Tablet: adjusted grids, spacing and navigation.
- Mobile: mobile navigation, one/two-column cards, responsive buttons, full-width sections, mobile-friendly chatbot and touch-friendly controls.
- No horizontal scrolling.

---

## 20. Accessibility & UX
- Readable text, good contrast, clear buttons, image alt text, keyboard-friendly controls where possible, visible focus states, touch-friendly controls and clear error messages.
- Include empty-cart and empty-search-result states.

---

## 21. Loading, Empty States & Animations
- Empty cart: “Your cart is feeling a little empty 🍨” with Explore Menu.
- No results: “Oops! We couldn't find that flavor.” with View All Flavors.
- Chatbot loading: animated typing dots and “ScoopBot is typing...”
- Use subtle product hover, button hover, cart-addition, chatbot opening, message and favorite animations.

---

## 22. Important Development Requirements
- The application must be frontend-only.
- Do not add a real database, backend server, authentication, real payment gateway, real order processing or external AI API unless specifically requested later.
- Use fictional mock data for products, reviews, orders, chatbot conversations and contact information.

---

## 23. Final User Experience
- Customer flow: Open website → Browse products → Search/filter → View product → Add to cart → Adjust quantity → Checkout → Chat with ScoopBot → Receive recommendations → Add recommended products to cart.
- The final website should feel like a real professional ice cream shop rather than a basic student project.

---

## 24. Definition of Done
- Home, Menu, Product Details, Cart, Checkout, Offers, About and Contact are complete.
- Search, category filters, product cards, quantity controls, checkout and navigation work.
- Chatbot opens/closes, responds to common questions, recommends products and allows recommended products to be added to cart.
- Chatbot and entire website work on desktop, tablet and mobile.
- Mock data is used, UI is polished, and no backend/database is required.

---

## 25. Final Design Direction
- Build with a premium, playful ice cream aesthetic: Cute + Colorful + Premium + Modern + Responsive + Interactive.
- The primary focus is a beautiful user experience and a highly responsive ScoopBot integrated naturally into the shopping experience.
